page('Your live explanation and code navigation','Use the short explanation first; open functions only when asked for more depth')
h('Opening explanation')
p('"How it works is by choosing where our entire hidden container begins. We support manual coordinates and a keyed mode. In keyed mode, the GUI passes my secret and settings to engine.protect. That calls derive_start in startloc.py, which uses HMAC-SHA256 with the secret as the key and the masked cover fingerprint, cover type and LSB depth as its data. The remainder modulo the number of units gives a valid starting position."')
h('What to click and say')
p('<b>1. Keyed image:</b> load cover_image.png, type a short message, choose 1 LSB and team-secret-2026. Protect into a separate output. Point at unit 358,456. Say: "This number is computed by derive_start; it is not a randomly stored coordinate."')
p('<b>2. Change the secret:</b> keep the same original cover and depth, use team-secret-2027 and another output. Point at 141,331. Say: "For these inputs, changing the secret changes the position. Reusing the same inputs repeats it."')
p('<b>3. Keyed Verify:</b> open the second output with Keyed, 1 LSB, team-secret-2027 and matching public key. Verify, then change only the verification secret to team-secret-2026 and repeat with scanning enabled. Say: "A valid container exists, but not at the expected position, so we get Wrong Start Location."')
p('<b>4. Manual comparison:</b> protect a separate image at (300, 300). Verify at (100, 100), then (300, 300). Say: "Manual mode directly converts coordinates into units. It does not use HMAC." For audio, the manual input is a frame index, such as 20,000.')
h('If the professor says show me the code')
table([['<b>Question</b>','<b>Open here</b>'],['Where is the GUI choice read?','app.py:457 p_run; mode and secret are passed to the engine.'],['Where is the decision keyed versus manual?','engine.py:116; keyed calls derive_start, manual uses manual_unit.'],['Where is the actual position calculated?','startloc.py:42 derive_start; crypto_utils.py:98 hmac_sha256.'],['Why is the fingerprint stable?','covers.py:37 mask table; :100 image hash; :183 audio hash.'],['Where are bits written?','engine.py:126; lsb.py:110 embed and :97 _wrapped_indices.'],['Where does the receiver calculate its expectation?','engine.py:208 derive_start call inside verify.'],['Where does Wrong Start Location come from?','engine.py:170 _locate and :276 location-mismatch check.']],[236,267])
p('<b>Closing limitation:</b> "The visible SVFY marker can be found by scanning, including by our own diagnostic tool. The keyed position avoids a fixed start but does not guarantee secrecy. AES-GCM protects message contents; the signature and hashes support authenticity and integrity."')
p('<b>Do not claim:</b> encryption of the coordinate, a new position on every run, a random gap after the header, or detection of every possible change to masked media bits. The project uses Python\'s HMAC implementation; describe your actual work and understanding accurately.')
